  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1200 PM EDT Sat Jun 20 2026\n\n- Chance of showers through Northeast Michigan late today\n\n A Weak trough continues to filter through the region today. While\nthere is not a lot of instability overall, A PV anomaly should\nallow for enough through northeastern and north central MI for \nisolated storms late this afternoon. The northwesterly flow will \nkeep temperatures cool with gusty winds upwards of 25 mph. \n \n- Showers Late Sunday into Monday\n\n So the upper level low that has been in discussion for the last\nfew days continues to waffle based on the upper level pattern.\n Some runs have shifted the trough further south, NAEFS specific\nhumidity and the EC ensembles continue has the upper level\nmoisture further northward in Lower Michigan. Timing remains a\nSunday evening into Monday morning event. '\n Areas along and south of the I 96 corridor should receive some\nrainfall. The question remains where the highest axis of\nprecipitation will be. The best moisture should remain in IN and\nOhio. QPF should range around a half an inch along I 96 down to 1\nto 1.5 inches along I 94 southward. \n \n- Showers and storms possible Midweek\n\nThe forecast remains fairly consistent ahead. Upper level low\nremains on track to drop southward across the Upper Midwest with\nthe low expected to track through Michigan Thursday. So mid week\nshowers and storms are possible with Highs trending closer to\nnormal with slightly  more warm air advection.",
